#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:4
msgid "CPS (Common Package Specification)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:8
msgid ""
"The `Common Package Specification (CPS) <https://cps-org.github.io/cps/>`_ "
"is an effort to create a standard, build-system agnostic, JSON description "
"of the binary packages of C and C++ libraries and applications: where the "
"headers and libraries are, which definitions have to be used, which other "
"packages and components are required, etc. It aims to replace the many "
"different and build-system specific ways to describe this information, like "
"CMake ``xxx-config.cmake`` files, ``.pc`` files for pkg-config, MSBuild "
"``.props`` files, and so on, improving the interoperability between package "
"managers and build systems. The specification is being developed "
"collaboratively by different tools and companies, including Kitware (CMake) "
"and JFrog (Conan)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:17
msgid ""
"CPS files are named ``<name>.cps``, and can have additional files for "
"specific configurations, like ``<name>@release.cps`` or "
"``<name>@debug.cps``. CMake (>=4.4) can both generate CPS files "
"(``install(PACKAGE_INFO <name> EXPORT <name>)``) and consume them with "
"``find_package()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:21
msgid ""
"The CPS support in Conan is **experimental**, it is evolving together with "
"the specification and with the CMake implementation, and it can have "
"breaking changes in future Conan versions. It requires CMake>=4.4 for the "
"CMake integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:27
msgid ""
"The :ref:`videos<videos>` section contains talks by Diego Rodriguez-Losada "
"about CPS and its Conan implementation: :ref:`std::cpp "
"2025<using_stdcpp2025_cps>`, an introduction to CPS, and :ref:`CppCon "
"2024<cppcon2024_cps>`, about a package specification and its implementation "
"in Conan. The earlier :ref:`CppCon 2023<cppcon2023_build_tools>` talk is "
"related, but predates the CPS standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:34
msgid "The ``CPSDeps`` generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:36
msgid ""
"Conan already has all the information that CPS files need in the "
"``package_info()`` method of every recipe: libraries, include directories, "
"definitions, system libraries, components, requirements between "
"components... This is the information that Conan generators use to create "
"``xxx-config.cmake``, ``.pc`` or ``.props`` files for the consumers. This is "
"the main advantage of the Conan approach: the ``CPSDeps`` generator can "
"create the CPS files for **any** package, including all the existing recipes "
"in ConanCenter, without requiring any change in those recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:43 ../../../integrations/cps.rst:104
#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:157
msgid "conanfile.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:43
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"\n"
"class Pkg(ConanFile):\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"compiler\", \"arch\", \"build_type\"\n"
"    requires = \"zlib/1.3.1\"\n"
"    generators = \"CPSDeps\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:53
msgid "It can also be used directly from the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:55
msgid "$ conan install --requires=zlib/1.3.1 -g CPSDeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:59
msgid ""
"The generator creates, inside the ``build/cps`` folder of the consumer, one "
"folder per binary configuration (named after the compiler, version, "
"architecture, C++ standard, build type and ``shared`` option, like "
"``msvc-193-x86_64-release``). Inside it, a ``cps`` folder contains one "
"``<name>.cps`` file for every dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:64
msgid ""
"build/cps/\n"
"├── cpsmap-msvc-193-x86_64-release.json\n"
"└── msvc-193-x86_64-release/\n"
"    └── cps/\n"
"        └── zlib.cps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:72
msgid ""
"The ``cpsmap-<configuration>.json`` file is a mapping from the name of every "
"dependency to the path of its ``.cps`` file, that can be used by other tools "
"to locate the files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:75
msgid ""
"If a package already contains its own ``<name>.cps`` file at the root of the "
"package folder (for example because it was built with CMake and it was "
"packaged, see the next section), then the generator will not create a new "
"file, but the mapping will point to the one in the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:81
msgid "Round trip with CMake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:83
msgid ""
"Recipes packaging CMake projects that generate CPS files (with "
"``install(PACKAGE_INFO)`` in CMake>=4.4) can feed the CPS information back "
"to Conan, so it can be used by consumers with **any** build system. This is "
"the \"round trip\": CMake generates the CPS file, Conan reads it and "
"populates the ``cpp_info``, and then Conan generators create the files for "
"the consumers' build system, which can be CMake or any other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:88 ../../../integrations/cps.rst:167
msgid "CMakeLists.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:88
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 4.4)\n"
"project(mypkg CXX)\n"
"\n"
"add_library(mypkg src/mypkg.cpp)\n"
"target_include_directories(mypkg PUBLIC\n"
"            $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>\n"
"            $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include>)\n"
"target_compile_definitions(mypkg PUBLIC FOO BAR=42)\n"
"set_target_properties(mypkg PROPERTIES PUBLIC_HEADER \"include/mypkg.h\")\n"
"\n"
"install(TARGETS mypkg EXPORT mypkg)\n"
"install(PACKAGE_INFO mypkg EXPORT mypkg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:104
msgid ""
"import glob\n"
"\n"
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.cps import CPS\n"
"from conan.tools.cmake import CMake, cmake_layout\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MypkgRecipe(ConanFile):\n"
"    name = \"mypkg\"\n"
"    version = \"0.1\"\n"
"    package_type = \"library\"\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"compiler\", \"build_type\", \"arch\"\n"
"    options = {\"shared\": [True, False], \"fPIC\": [True, False]}\n"
"    default_options = {\"shared\": False, \"fPIC\": True}\n"
"\n"
"    exports_sources = \"CMakeLists.txt\", \"src/*\", \"include/*\"\n"
"    implements = [\"auto_shared_fpic\"]\n"
"    generators = \"CMakeToolchain\"\n"
"\n"
"    def layout(self):\n"
"        cmake_layout(self)\n"
"\n"
"    def build(self):\n"
"        cmake = CMake(self)\n"
"        cmake.configure()\n"
"        cmake.build()\n"
"\n"
"    def package(self):\n"
"        cmake = CMake(self)\n"
"        cmake.install()\n"
"\n"
"    def package_info(self):\n"
"        # Locate the CPS file that CMake installed in the package, and\n"
"        # translate it to the Conan \"cpp_info\" model\n"
"        cps_file = glob.glob(\"**/mypkg.cps\", recursive=True)[0]\n"
"        self.cpp_info = CPS.load(cps_file).to_conan()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:144
msgid ""
"``CPS.load()`` reads the ``mypkg.cps`` file, together with the "
"``mypkg@release.cps`` or ``mypkg@debug.cps`` files that might exist next to "
"it, and ``to_conan()`` converts them to a ``cpp_info`` object (with "
"components, if the CPS file defines them). The package is still using the "
"standard Conan model, so it can be consumed with any generator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:150
msgid "Consuming from CMake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:152
msgid ""
"When the consumer uses ``CMakeConfigDeps`` and sets the ``cmake_find_mode`` "
"property of the package to ``none``, Conan will not generate a ``<name>-"
"config.cmake`` file. If the package contains a ``<name>.cps`` file, the "
"generator will detect it and make CMake ``find_package()`` find that CPS "
"file in the package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:157
msgid ""
"from conan.tools.cmake import CMakeConfigDeps\n"
"\n"
"def generate(self):\n"
"    deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"    deps.set_property(\"mypkg\", \"cmake_find_mode\", \"none\")\n"
"    deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:167
msgid ""
"find_package(mypkg CONFIG REQUIRED)\n"
"target_link_libraries(example mypkg::mypkg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:173
msgid ""
"The CPS file will be the one that CMake generated, the same that a user not "
"using Conan would get from the installed package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:177
msgid "Consuming from other build systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:179
msgid ""
"Because ``package_info()`` populated the ``cpp_info`` from the CPS file, the "
"package can be consumed from build systems other than CMake, using the usual "
"Conan generators, for example ``MSBuildDeps`` for MSBuild and Visual Studio, "
"``PkgConfigDeps`` for Meson and Autotools, and others. This means that a "
"project can use CMake and CPS for building and describing the library, and "
"still be consumed transparently by consumers using MSBuild, without any "
"extra work by the package creator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:185
msgid "conanfile.py of the consumer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:185
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"\n"
"class Consumer(ConanFile):\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"compiler\", \"arch\", \"build_type\"\n"
"    requires = \"mypkg/0.1\"\n"
"    generators = \"MSBuildDeps\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:197
msgid ""
"The recipe above is just using the generic conversion "
"``CPS.load(...).to_conan()``. Recipes can still define or complete the "
"``cpp_info`` manually in ``package_info()``, when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:202
msgid "Current limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:204
msgid ""
"The support is experimental, and the generated information and the API of "
"``conan.cps`` can change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:205
msgid ""
"The CPS specification itself is still evolving, so only a subset of its "
"fields is supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/cps.rst:206
msgid "The CMake integration requires CMake>=4.4."
msgstr ""
